The best tutorial for your use case

Since you're writing a layer rather than an application, I highly recommend reading through https://vulkan-tutorial.com with a specific focus on these chapters:

Instance
Physical device
Logical device and queues
Swap chain
Image views
Graphics pipeline
Command buffers
Synchronization

You can ignore the window creation parts—they're not relevant because the application (or DXVK) already creates the window and surface. Concentrate on understanding the rendering objects and the per-frame flow, since that's exactly what your layer will interact with.